WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.990
- Wow, that was fast.

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:06.670
This was like this big,
less than two minutes ago.

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.920
- [Narrator] This is
the Eight Sleep Pod Pro,

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.930
one of the top rated smart
beds on the market right now.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:14.360
And what exactly makes
a smart bed so smart?

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.830
This one comes equipped
with sensor technology,

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.950
an app that gathers sleep data,

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.270
and a water hub for temperature control.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.119
- I feel overwhelmed already.

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:24.000
(laughing together)

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.340
That's why you're here.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.460
- [Narrator] This is Dr. Wendy Troxel,

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.020
she's a clinical psychologist,

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:31.020
specially trained in sleep medicine,

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.210
which basically means she's
an expert in all things sleep.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.580
- For the past 16 years or so

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.730
I've spent most of my
waking hours thinking about

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.400
and studying sleep,

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.430
and treating individuals and couples

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:45.580
who present with sleep related issues.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.440
- [Narrator] So then
who better to test this,

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.240
the Eight Sleep Pod Pro?

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.220
- I'm a bit of a skeptic, honestly,

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.060
when it comes to smart beds

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:57.230
and overly fancy sort of
technology in general,

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.530
when it comes to the bed and the bedroom.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:01.010
- [Narrator] Let's see if this smart bed

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:04.230
can win her over and help
us decide is a smart bed

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.617
really smarter for your sleep?

00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:10.367
(gentle instrumental music)

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.790
Spending more time at
home during the pandemic

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:16.290
has led a lot of people
to upgrade their bedrooms,

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.520
buying mattresses that
incorporate technology

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.490
to improve the quality of their sleep.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:23.330
That's why we're testing
the Eight Sleep Pod Pro.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.500
But why did we choose this smart bed?

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.880
A few reasons, it has the most
common smart bed features,

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.050
sleep tracking and temperature control,

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:32.960
but it also has a smart alarm,

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.640
which silently wakes you up
with chest level vibration

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.510
and gradual temperature change.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:40.120
It's also considered a mid range smart bed

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:43.100
with the king size running about $3,500.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:48.100
Smart beds can cost anywhere
from 1,500 to over $100,000.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.133
- I have to say,

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:53.410
I am completely naive to the
whole smart bed experience,

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:55.010
I have never slept on one.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:57.440
- [Narrator] First, Dr.
Troxel assessed how easy

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:58.810
it is to set up the bed.

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:01.520
- I did not know that it was
going to be a bed in a box.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.180
It says this is 80 pounds.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.840
We were able to hire movers,
which is very helpful,

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:07.283
these are heavy boxes.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:10.030
- [Narrator] While Eight Sleep

00:02:10.881 --> 00:02:11.714
doesn't offer white glove service,

00:02:11.714 --> 00:02:13.970
you can video call one
of their product experts

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.709
to help with setup.

00:02:15.709 --> 00:02:16.620
- Hey, how's it going?
- Good.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.611
Thanks for meeting with us.

00:02:18.611 --> 00:02:20.271
The setup itself, I have to say,

00:02:20.271 --> 00:02:23.350
was a bit daunting and it
felt very medicalized to me.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.330
- [Product Expert] You're
gonna want to sneak it through

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:28.060
in the midst, so like
down behind the mattress.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:31.010
- I mean, the fact that there's
a tube coming out of my bed

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:34.407
kind of rubbed me the
wrong way a little bit.

00:02:34.407 --> 00:02:35.814
(zipper whirring)

00:02:35.814 --> 00:02:36.810
(water splashing)

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.370
(gentle instrumental music)

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:39.570
So this was kind of cool.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:42.760
First it asked me what
side of the bed I sleep on,

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.600
then I can also invite my partner.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.690
With the help of the tech
support from Eight Sleep

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:50.380
it went relatively very smoothly,

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.950
it was not instantaneous by any means.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.210
- [Product Expert] And after 90 minutes

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:57.602
it will be quiet and
perfect and ready to use.

00:02:57.602 --> 00:02:59.420
- [Narrator] Next, Dr. Troxel
reviewed the bed for comfort.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:02.010
She and her husband slept
on it for three nights.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:03.600
- You know, it doesn't
have any of the other bells

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.620
and whistles in terms of
contouring or things like that,

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.120
that others smart beds have,

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.180
but it is certainly comfortable.

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:14.210
My husband probably preferred the firmness

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:15.890
of the mattress more than I do.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:19.410
Comfort is an entirely
subjective experience.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:22.250
And this is why some
smart beds, not this one,

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:26.310
do you have individualized
firmness preferences.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:30.110
I did notice that a times in
the night it was quite cool,

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:33.600
and then in the morning when
I was waking up it warmed up,

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.170
because that's how I
had set my preferences.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:37.580
And I enjoyed.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.550
- [Narrator] Finally, Dr. Troxel assessed

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:42.650
the effectiveness of the beds
sleep tracking technology.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:44.220
- Well according to this app,

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.100
last night I was a perfect sleeper.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:51.370
I got a 100 on my sleep score,
but to be honest with you,

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:53.283
I didn't get a good night of sleep.

00:03:53.283 --> 00:03:55.621
(machinery whirring)

00:03:55.621 --> 00:03:57.390
This is the noise that
we are currently hearing,

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.240
I have no idea why.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:02.570
This was really disruptive
to my sleep, in fact,

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:06.970
I know that I was awake
for at least 30 minutes

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.090
in the middle of the night.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:12.170
We did have to do a
repriming of the hub today.

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:15.680
So hopefully that may have
resolved the noise issue.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:18.930
The noise, that was virtually
non-existent last night.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.600
But when I looked at the
metrics more closely,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.570
I saw that there were clearly errors

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.730
in how they were scoring my sleep.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:28.740
You do have the opportunity
to edit your metrics,

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.970
and I did so this morning by indicating

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.580
that I wasn't even trying
to fall asleep until

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:37.440
about a half hour after the
bed had measured me sleeping,

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.960
and that I also woke
up about a half an hour

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:42.020
before I actually got out of bed.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:43.860
- [Narrator] So after
trying out the smart bed,

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:47.600
does Dr. Troxel think it's
worth the $3,500 price tag?

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:51.170
- I'm going to give this mattress
overall three star rating.

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:54.360
I did enjoy the temperature
control feature,

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.960
and for partners who share a bed,

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.220
I think this feature of
having a non noise alarm

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:02.460
is really nice.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.330
And the third thing I liked about the bed

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:06.850
was the technology support we received.

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:10.360
Now in terms of the cons,
every time my husband moved,

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:13.600
I could not only feel the
mattress itself shifting,

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:17.750
but I could also feel the
fabric in the mattress cover,

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.120
that would shift as well.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.900
The other thing that I was
not particularly pleased

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.690
about was the overall setup.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:27.120
Now the third downside was
the accuracy of the metrics.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:29.440
I can tell you from my own data,

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:32.940
that these metrics were
not entirely accurate.

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:35.130
An important caveat of my review

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:38.410
is that I only tested this
bed over three nights.

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:40.190
So my experience of the bed

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:42.750
may very likely change over time.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.910
- [Narrator] Eight Sleep
said it takes about one week

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.790
for the pod to acclimate to your body,

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.500
and the sleep fitness scores become

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.340
more reflective of your sleep quality

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:51.510
the more you use it.

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:53.480
With regard to the noise from the hub,

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.950
a spokesperson said, it
typically occurs when there

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.430
is still air in the system

00:05:57.430 --> 00:06:00.580
and all the unit needs is
another round of priming.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.543
- Where do you plug it in?
- That's a good question.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.510
A bed that plugs in.
- But that's not a water cord,

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:10.117
that's a plug.
- Oh.

00:06:10.117 --> 00:06:10.950
(laughing together)

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:11.880
I do you have a PhD.

00:06:12.932 --> 00:06:16.682
(gentle instrumental music)

